7. Error Function and Fresnel Integrals
Mathematical Properties
7.1. Error Function
Definitions
7.1.1 \text{erf} z=\frac{2}{\sqrt{\pi}}\int_{0}^{z}e^{-t^2}dt
7.1.2 \text{erfc} z=\frac{2}{\sqrt{\pi}}\int_{z}^{\infty}e^{-t^2}dt=1-\text{erf}z
7.1.3  w(z)=e^{-t^2}\left(1+\frac{2i}{\sqrt{\pi}}\int_{0}^{z}e^{t^2}dt\right)=e^{- t^2}\text{erfc}\,\left(-iz\right)
In 7.1.2 the path of integration is subject to the restriction arg t-to with |a|<\frac{\pi}{4} as t-to along the path. (a=\frac{\pi}{4} is permissible if Rt' remains bounded to the left.) Integral Representation
7.1.4  w(z)=\frac{i}{\pi}\int_{-\infty}^{\infty}\frac{e^{-t^2}dt}{z-t}=\frac{2iz}{\pi}\int_{0}^{\infty}\frac{e^{-t^2}dt}{z^{2}-t^2}\quad(\mathcal{I}z>0)
Series Expansions
7.1.5 \text{erf} z=\frac{2}{\sqrt{\pi}}\sum_{n=0}^{\infty}\frac{(-1)^{n}z^{2n+1}}{n!(2n+1)}\]
7.1.6 =\frac{2}{\sqrt{\pi}}\ e^{-t^2}\sum_{n=0}^{\infty}\frac{2^{n}}{1:3\cdot\ldots(2n+1)}z^{2n+1}\]
7.1.7 =\sqrt{2}\sum_{n=0}^{\infty}(-1)^{n}[I_{2n+1/2}(z^{2})-I_{2n+3/2}(z^{2})]
7.1.8  w(z)=\sum_{n=0}^{\infty}\frac{(iz)^{n}}{\Gamma\left(\frac{n}{2}+1\right)}
For I_{n-1}(x), see chapter 10.
Symmetry Relations
7.1.9 \text{erf}\,\left(-z\right)=-\text{erf}\,z
7.1.10 \text{erf}\,\overline{z}=\overline{\text{erf}}\,z
7.1.11  w(-z)=2e^{-t^2}-w(z)
7.1.12  w(-z)=w(-z)